  "title": "Erdős Problem #911",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $\\hat{R}(G)$ denote the size Ramsey number, the minimal number of edges $m$ such that there is a graph $H$ with $m$ edges that is Ramsey for $G$.\nIs there a function $f$ such that $f(x)/x\\to \\infty$ as $x\\to \\infty$ such that, for all large $C$, if $G$ is a graph with $n$ vertices and $e\\geq Cn$ edges then $ \\hat{R}(G) > f(C) e? $ \",\n    \"difficulty\": \"L1\"\n},{",
